r": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011BCYiKrDxNMpBGpKsnyBMg", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["honor_retry_after", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 380637, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011BCYiKrDxNMpBGpKsnyBMg", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 384523, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and the pull request is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding. That broke `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even`.\n- **Fix:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101).\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory lookup (\"Unknown advisory\"), so the expected behaviour comes from the test and the docstring alone. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011k8EKtsSM7mcufy8MzAfYy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VdVt14UJQRrY5SDP1TTvxN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014eZiSRbF9Qk5qPe9vA4ySx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KeeF8EvzLanqWh6FBYCQ8C", "caller": {"type":