 null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and the pull request is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding. That broke `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even`.\n- **Fix:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101).\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory lookup (\"Unknown advisory\"), so the expected behaviour comes from the test and the docstring alone. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}